- ### Refund (race condition, pay-now only)
- If a refund is issued, tell the customer: "We're sorry — your slot was taken by another booking right as your payment processed. A full refund has been issued. Let me find you another time."
- ### Pay-on-completion no-show
- Pay-on-completion relies on the customer being there. If they ask to cancel, they can email **connor@getcolby.com** at least 24 hours before the slot. Persistent no-shows may be required to pre-pay on future bookings.
- ### Lost credentials
- If the customer's username and password aren't in memory (new device, wiped session), don't ask the customer to recite them — they were saved silently and the customer was never shown them. Just run `initiate_booking` without credentials; the server will return `credentials_required` with a fresh checkout URL, the customer re-verifies, and `claim_credentials` refreshes memory. The saved card isn't re-charged; the re-verification is the one-time $120 for the cleaning itself.
